6. INTEGRATION, TESTING AND DEPENDENCIES

The implemented backend functionality still requires UI integration, joint va=
lidation and defect resolution. Expected work includes changes to:

- Business.controller.js, TBS.controller.js, service/model configuration and =
existing fragments.
- Gateway contracts and error handling where integration exposes differences.
- ABAP Unit and integration-test scenarios.
- Test data, authorization scenarios and reconciliation against legacy behavi=
our.

There is no reliable separate remaining estimate for the complete integration=
 phase without agreed interface contracts, test scope and ownership. Configur=
ation end-to-end testing is currently blocked by the dashboard dependency.

Consequently, a backend item marked "implemented" should not be read as "inte=
grated, business-tested and ready for production."

