se activities are not separately quantified in the supplied plan and should n=
ot be assumed to have zero effort.

8. PLANNING CONCLUSION

The inventory shows that DAS delivery comprises considerably more than the in=
dividually named application tasks: it includes shared backend logic, service=
s, replication, DDIC objects, automated tests and integration infrastructure.

The figures above provide a transparent planning baseline. They do not establ=
ish actual development hours incurred or a confirmed variance against budget.=
 That comparison requires recorded time entries and an agreed mapping between=
 functional tasks and shared technical work.

